1
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:10,480
If you knew the truth,

2
00:03:11,200 --> 00:03:13,280
you'd probably cry your eyes out.

3
00:03:13,880 --> 00:03:16,640
If you want to know,
investigate it yourself.

4
00:03:16,720 --> 00:03:18,280
The way she threatened me just now…

5
00:03:18,360 --> 00:03:21,360
It sounded like
there's some secret I don't know.

6
00:03:22,040 --> 00:03:23,640
You know why

7
00:03:23,720 --> 00:03:25,520
I agreed to claim Papang as my son.

8
00:03:26,120 --> 00:03:27,360
Just because I'm leaving…

9
00:03:27,440 --> 00:03:28,280
PREVIOUSLY

10
00:03:28,360 --> 00:03:31,520
…doesn't mean I'm giving up. I'll be back.

11
00:03:31,600 --> 00:03:35,040
I'm sorry. I didn't mean to do it.

12
00:03:35,120 --> 00:03:38,480
I'm the one who told Hathaya
to bring her grandmother here.

13
00:03:47,280 --> 00:03:48,760
Is this okay for you, Grandma?

14
00:03:49,360 --> 00:03:53,400
At my age, it doesn't matter
whether the room is big or small.

15
00:03:55,800 --> 00:03:59,200
As long as I have a roof
over my head, that's enough.

16
00:03:59,840 --> 00:04:01,320
And as long as I get to be with you,

17
00:04:01,400 --> 00:04:04,760
I could even live under a bridge.

18
00:04:06,920 --> 00:04:10,000
This feels so good.

19
00:04:12,360 --> 00:04:14,160
Thank you, sweetheart.

20
00:04:14,240 --> 00:04:16,640
You've done everything for me.

21
00:04:16,720 --> 00:04:19,320
I should be the one thanking you.

22
00:04:19,399 --> 00:04:23,560
I grew up to be who I am
because of everything you taught me.

23
00:04:27,840 --> 00:04:30,360
If Hathai had even a fraction
of what you have,

24
00:04:31,040 --> 00:04:33,120
maybe our lives
wouldn't have been so difficult.

25
00:04:35,880 --> 00:04:39,280
Grandma, have you heard anything from Mom?

26
00:04:39,880 --> 00:04:43,960
Not since I left the hospital.
I haven't heard a thing from her.

27
00:04:46,960 --> 00:04:48,840
Don't talk about your mom anymore.

28
00:04:49,760 --> 00:04:51,680
We all have to bear with our own choices.

29
00:04:51,760 --> 00:04:53,640
Let's just love each other.

30
00:04:54,200 --> 00:04:55,080
That's right.

31
00:05:00,280 --> 00:05:02,560
How much longer
are we going to live like this?

32
00:05:03,280 --> 00:05:05,040
We can't even go anywhere.

33
00:05:05,760 --> 00:05:08,240
If I'd known, I never would've
opened that brothel with you.

34
00:05:08,320 --> 00:05:10,560
Did I force you to do it?

35
00:05:10,640 --> 00:05:13,680
You wanted money. You wanted to get rich
the easy way. Stop complaining.

36
00:05:13,760 --> 00:05:17,920
Then what can we do? I can't live
like this for another ten years.

37
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:20,960
I'm asking someone powerful
to pull strings for us.

38
00:05:24,400 --> 00:05:25,520
Yes, sir.

39
00:05:26,520 --> 00:05:30,040
All right, sir.
I'll come see you right away.

40
00:05:30,120 --> 00:05:31,520
Yes, sir.

41
00:05:33,160 --> 00:05:36,680
He took care of everything.
Bring the money.

42
00:05:37,280 --> 00:05:40,680
There's 200,000 baht left.
I was going to save it to pay Mom back.

43
00:05:40,760 --> 00:05:42,920
What? You want to go to prison?

44
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:44,000
-Give it to me.
-Let go.

45
00:05:44,080 --> 00:05:45,600
Give it here.

46
00:05:45,680 --> 00:05:47,280
Go take a shower,

47
00:05:47,360 --> 00:05:49,240
and make yourself look nice.

48
00:05:49,320 --> 00:05:52,120
We're just returning his money.
You can go by yourself.

49
00:05:52,200 --> 00:05:53,560
I'm not going. I'm staying here.

50
00:05:53,640 --> 00:05:58,240
Stop being difficult. If you want
someone to help us, we both have to go.

51
00:05:58,840 --> 00:06:00,320
Are you coming or not?

52
00:06:00,400 --> 00:06:01,520
Fine.

53
00:06:01,600 --> 00:06:03,080
Go.

54
00:06:03,160 --> 00:06:04,480
Hurry up.

55
00:06:15,280 --> 00:06:18,160
He's waiting inside. Give him this money.

56
00:06:18,240 --> 00:06:20,480
He'll take care of everything.

57
00:06:23,840 --> 00:06:25,160
How is he going to do that?

58
00:06:25,240 --> 00:06:28,000
He'll find a scapegoat
to take the blame for us.

59
00:06:28,080 --> 00:06:31,880
After that, we can go back
to living comfortably.

60
00:06:31,960 --> 00:06:33,600
Come on. Go in.

61
00:06:34,640 --> 00:06:35,680
Where are you going?

62
00:06:36,280 --> 00:06:39,160
I'm going downstairs
for a cigarette. I'll be back.

63
00:06:39,240 --> 00:06:40,480
Wait.

64
00:06:41,200 --> 00:06:43,600
You can smoke later.
Come inside with me first.

65
00:06:47,920 --> 00:06:49,480
This is really all I have, sir.

66
00:06:51,520 --> 00:06:53,720
I'm not too concerned about the money.

67
00:06:55,240 --> 00:06:57,280
We help each other if we can.

68
00:06:57,360 --> 00:07:00,840
So this is all over now, right, sir?

69
00:07:01,440 --> 00:07:02,680
I settled it with the police.

70
00:07:02,760 --> 00:07:05,760
Thank you so much, sir.

71
00:07:07,320 --> 00:07:10,680
Then I won't take up
any more of your time.

72
00:07:11,440 --> 00:07:12,960
I'll excuse myself.

73
00:07:13,480 --> 00:07:15,080
Where are you rushing off to?

74
00:07:16,360 --> 00:07:17,840
Your husband says you massage well.

75
00:07:19,040 --> 00:07:22,600
I've been running around pulling strings
for you until my whole body aches.

76
00:07:23,440 --> 00:07:24,680
Come give me a massage.

77
00:07:25,760 --> 00:07:29,640
Go on. Give him a massage. I'm going
downstairs to smoke in the lobby.

78
00:07:31,760 --> 00:07:32,600
Stay here with me.

79
00:07:33,880 --> 00:07:34,920
Why?

80
00:07:36,040 --> 00:07:37,240
You don't trust me?

81
00:07:38,960 --> 00:07:42,160
No, sir. It's just…

82
00:07:42,240 --> 00:07:43,880
I don't think it would be appropriate.

83
00:07:43,960 --> 00:07:45,440
You're right.

84
00:07:46,200 --> 00:07:47,800
A married woman

85
00:07:47,880 --> 00:07:51,520
shouldn't be alone in a room
with another man. How about this?

86
00:07:52,920 --> 00:07:55,440
Stay here, Big. Don't go anywhere.

87
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:58,000
Yes, sir.

88
00:07:59,120 --> 00:08:00,920
Go on. Give him a massage.

89
00:08:02,200 --> 00:08:03,320
Go.

90
00:08:18,440 --> 00:08:20,240
Right here.

91
00:08:22,680 --> 00:08:23,600
Sir.

92
00:08:24,440 --> 00:08:27,640
I think I should leave now.

93
00:08:27,720 --> 00:08:30,400
Hey. Don't be rude.

94
00:08:30,480 --> 00:08:32,640
He went to all this trouble
to save us from prison.

95
00:08:32,720 --> 00:08:34,960
But he crossed the line first.

96
00:08:35,039 --> 00:08:36,520
And how can you be okay with this?

97
00:08:36,600 --> 00:08:38,280
He helps us, we help him.

98
00:08:38,360 --> 00:08:41,520
Didn't your mother
ever teach you to repay a favor?

99
00:08:41,600 --> 00:08:45,000
This isn't repaying a favor.
This is disgusting.

100
00:08:45,080 --> 00:08:48,200
Disgusting or survival.
Which one are you choosing?

101
00:08:48,280 --> 00:08:51,560
-Move. I'm leaving.
-Stop.

102
00:08:53,320 --> 00:08:54,480
Big.

103
00:08:54,560 --> 00:08:55,880
Stay here!

104
00:08:55,960 --> 00:08:57,640
Let me go.

105
00:08:57,720 --> 00:09:00,800
Let me go. Somebody help me!

106
00:09:10,040 --> 00:09:12,360
Breakfast is ready, Grandpa.

107
00:09:12,440 --> 00:09:14,720
Chef Duangjai made it herself.

108
00:09:17,280 --> 00:09:18,800
After you eat,

109
00:09:18,880 --> 00:09:22,240
drink this herbal medicine.
It's good for your bones.

110
00:09:22,320 --> 00:09:25,960
I guarantee you won't have
aching joints or body pain.

111
00:09:26,040 --> 00:09:27,880
I drink it myself,

112
00:09:27,960 --> 00:09:30,400
so I can guarantee it works.

113
00:09:30,480 --> 00:09:32,920
If it doesn't,
I'll give you your money back.

114
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:35,480
Oh.

115
00:09:35,560 --> 00:09:36,640
Sorry.

116
00:09:36,720 --> 00:09:38,840
Please, go ahead and eat.

117
00:09:38,920 --> 00:09:41,440
Come eat with me.

118
00:09:41,520 --> 00:09:45,200
That's all right. You eat first.
I'll eat in the kitchen later.

119
00:09:45,840 --> 00:09:47,400
No.

120
00:09:48,440 --> 00:09:50,240
You have to eat here with me.

121
00:09:50,840 --> 00:09:52,240
You're serious?

122
00:09:58,200 --> 00:10:01,280
Ann, give me a big plate of rice.

123
00:10:01,360 --> 00:10:04,160
Of course, Grandma Duangjai.

124
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:11,920
Would you like to go anywhere, sir?
I can take you.

125
00:10:13,600 --> 00:10:17,640
I just wanted some fresh air.
I don't want to go anywhere.

126
00:10:18,800 --> 00:10:21,840
By the way, where are
Duangjai and Hathaya?

127
00:10:21,920 --> 00:10:24,080
They're over there.

128
00:10:25,080 --> 00:10:26,640
Planting roses.

129
00:10:27,320 --> 00:10:30,800
Grandma, you don't have to do that.
There are gardeners here.

130
00:10:31,840 --> 00:10:34,880
The gardeners have their own work to do.

131
00:10:34,960 --> 00:10:36,640
I want to help.

132
00:10:37,680 --> 00:10:39,640
Do you remember what I taught you?

133
00:10:40,440 --> 00:10:42,600
If you live under someone else's roof,

134
00:10:42,680 --> 00:10:45,680
don't sit around doing nothing.

135
00:10:46,440 --> 00:10:48,800
Of course I remember.

136
00:10:48,880 --> 00:10:52,200
When you're old, seeing beautiful things

137
00:10:53,080 --> 00:10:55,040
brightens your heart.

138
00:10:55,120 --> 00:10:57,960
Roses smell nice too.

139
00:10:58,040 --> 00:11:02,240
You can put them in a vase for Grandpa.
Doesn't that sound good?

140
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:05,840
It does. Then I'll help you.

141
00:11:05,920 --> 00:11:07,040
Good.

142
00:11:13,440 --> 00:11:14,360
What are you doing?

143
00:11:15,240 --> 00:11:16,800
Are you teasing me?

144
00:11:19,240 --> 00:11:20,360
Take this.

145
00:11:20,440 --> 00:11:22,200
You're washing this shirt for me, Grandma.

146
00:11:22,280 --> 00:11:24,080
Why are you like this, Grandma?

147
00:11:34,160 --> 00:11:36,640
It's been long since
I saw you laugh like this, sir.

148
00:11:38,960 --> 00:11:40,200
You're right.

149
00:11:41,440 --> 00:11:44,440
I'd almost forgotten
what my own laughter sounded like.

150
00:11:46,040 --> 00:11:50,680
I think Hathaya and Grandma Duangjai

151
00:11:50,760 --> 00:11:54,640
are going to make you happy
and keep you laughing every day.

152
00:11:58,960 --> 00:12:01,320
Hathaya's life would probably
have been more fulfilling

153
00:12:01,400 --> 00:12:03,960
and much better if she hadn't had
a mother like Hathai.

154
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:24,080
Hey!

155
00:12:24,160 --> 00:12:27,600
I checked. Neither of our names
is connected to the brothel raid anymore.

156
00:12:27,680 --> 00:12:29,600
You did a great job.

157
00:12:30,200 --> 00:12:33,200
I found a new location. I've already
taken care of the local police.

158
00:12:33,280 --> 00:12:36,000
We'll be opening another brothel soon.

159
00:12:37,320 --> 00:12:38,680
I'm not doing it anymore.

160
00:12:39,680 --> 00:12:42,160
And go find plenty of girls.

161
00:12:42,240 --> 00:12:45,200
As many as possible.
Students and working women too.

162
00:12:54,160 --> 00:12:55,440
Haven't you learned anything?

163
00:12:56,880 --> 00:12:58,560
I won't do wrong with you anymore.

164
00:12:58,640 --> 00:13:00,520
What's wrong about it?

165
00:13:00,600 --> 00:13:03,760
If people want to buy, someone
has to sell. We're just the middlemen.

166
00:13:03,840 --> 00:13:06,160
That kind of thinking is exactly why

167
00:13:06,240 --> 00:13:08,240
you're willing to sell your own wife.

168
00:13:08,320 --> 00:13:11,400
A wife isn't something
you put on an altar and worship.

169
00:13:11,480 --> 00:13:13,840
If you're my wife, you help me make money.

170
00:13:13,920 --> 00:13:15,400
You pimp!

171
00:13:15,480 --> 00:13:16,600
I'm done.

172
00:13:16,680 --> 00:13:18,080
Bitch!

173
00:13:19,400 --> 00:13:21,200
You came clinging to me.

174
00:13:21,280 --> 00:13:23,360
You hit on me because of my money and car.

175
00:13:23,440 --> 00:13:25,120
You've gotten plenty from me.

176
00:13:25,200 --> 00:13:27,800
Now it's time for you to pay me back.

177
00:13:30,520 --> 00:13:31,800
We're done.

178
00:13:32,440 --> 00:13:34,520
Do whatever you want.

179
00:13:34,600 --> 00:13:35,560
I'm out.

180
00:13:35,640 --> 00:13:36,880
Hey.

181
00:13:37,520 --> 00:13:40,440
Remember this.

182
00:13:40,520 --> 00:13:42,960
Whether you stay or go,
your life depends on me.

183
00:13:43,040 --> 00:13:46,160
You've taken plenty from me.

184
00:13:46,240 --> 00:13:49,840
Now you'll work to pay me back.
And if you try to run,

185
00:13:49,920 --> 00:13:51,960
you're dead. Understand?

186
00:13:55,560 --> 00:13:57,240
Don't go anywhere.

187
00:14:11,160 --> 00:14:12,640
Grandma.

188
00:14:12,720 --> 00:14:13,840
What are you doing?

189
00:14:13,920 --> 00:14:15,240
Writing down lottery numbers?

190
00:14:17,640 --> 00:14:18,880
No.

191
00:14:18,960 --> 00:14:20,640
I'm trying to figure out

192
00:14:20,720 --> 00:14:23,320
what to cook for your grandpa tomorrow.

193
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:25,960
But I still can't decide.

194
00:14:26,040 --> 00:14:29,680
I want to make something special.

195
00:14:30,800 --> 00:14:34,280
If you want to impress someone
from Bangkok, you'll have to come with me.

196
00:14:35,120 --> 00:14:36,880
Where are you taking me?

197
00:14:36,960 --> 00:14:40,360
I'm going to show you
what people in Bangkok like to eat.

198
00:14:41,640 --> 00:14:44,360
Would that be all right?
I don't want to impose.

199
00:14:44,440 --> 00:14:45,600
What?

200
00:14:45,680 --> 00:14:47,240
-Huh?
-Let's go.

201
00:14:48,520 --> 00:14:51,600
Well, Grandma Duangjai, a lady like you

202
00:14:51,680 --> 00:14:54,520
shouldn't be holding
onto a man like that. That isn't proper.

203
00:14:54,600 --> 00:14:55,680
Oh.

204
00:14:56,640 --> 00:14:59,280
Holding a man's arm isn't proper?

205
00:15:00,600 --> 00:15:01,640
Then,

206
00:15:01,720 --> 00:15:02,880
I'll kiss his cheek.

207
00:15:04,320 --> 00:15:05,600
Grandma!

208
00:15:05,680 --> 00:15:07,120
Now we've broken every custom.

209
00:15:07,200 --> 00:15:09,160
Then what am I supposed to do?

210
00:15:09,240 --> 00:15:12,160
Then I have to… kiss you back.

211
00:15:13,960 --> 00:15:16,360
And now you have to formally
ask for my hand.

212
00:15:16,960 --> 00:15:21,480
Oh, no. I don't have any money.
You'll just have to take me instead.

213
00:15:21,560 --> 00:15:24,040
Oh, you two.

214
00:15:24,120 --> 00:15:27,120
Come on.

215
00:15:27,200 --> 00:15:29,600
Go ahead and hug.
Don't let go of each other.

216
00:15:34,400 --> 00:15:37,440
DARA POCHANA

217
00:15:44,680 --> 00:15:48,800
The food is good, the atmosphere is nice,
and most importantly, the prices are good.

218
00:15:49,640 --> 00:15:50,800
Made-to-order stall always have

219
00:15:50,880 --> 00:15:52,720
a lot of dishes like this.

220
00:15:52,800 --> 00:15:53,960
Grandma,

221
00:15:54,040 --> 00:15:57,240
have you figured out what you want
to cook for Grandpa tomorrow?

222
00:15:59,320 --> 00:16:01,280
Tom yum goong sounds good.

223
00:16:01,960 --> 00:16:03,560
So does stir-fried curry paste.

224
00:16:04,280 --> 00:16:06,600
And ginger chicken is healthy too.

225
00:16:06,680 --> 00:16:09,040
Everything looks good.

226
00:16:09,120 --> 00:16:10,360
I can't decide.

227
00:16:10,440 --> 00:16:14,600
That's okay. If you can't choose,
make all of them.

228
00:16:14,680 --> 00:16:18,920
Your cooking is delicious anyway.

229
00:16:19,880 --> 00:16:23,280
My granddaughter sure knows
how to flatter me.

230
00:16:32,280 --> 00:16:33,280
Do you like that?

231
00:16:34,200 --> 00:16:35,040
I do.

232
00:16:46,600 --> 00:16:47,840
I mean…

233
00:16:47,920 --> 00:16:50,400
I like

234
00:16:50,480 --> 00:16:53,840
your cooking. You're a great cook.

235
00:16:53,920 --> 00:16:55,000
Sure.

236
00:16:59,080 --> 00:17:01,520
Let's eat. What should we try first?

237
00:17:11,560 --> 00:17:12,480
You first.

238
00:17:14,079 --> 00:17:15,119
No, you go ahead.

239
00:17:15,200 --> 00:17:17,119
It's fine. You first.

240
00:17:17,200 --> 00:17:19,280
I'm not that hungry.

241
00:17:19,359 --> 00:17:20,800
Just eat.

242
00:17:22,240 --> 00:17:23,680
This one is really good.

243
00:17:23,760 --> 00:17:24,720
Then eat it.

244
00:17:24,800 --> 00:17:27,000
You're my guest. I have to give you some.

245
00:17:27,079 --> 00:17:29,440
It's okay. I can survive.

246
00:17:33,520 --> 00:17:36,920
Hathai, I rented a building already.

247
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:38,760
You can start finding women for us.

248
00:17:45,520 --> 00:17:46,720
Hathai.

249
00:17:50,920 --> 00:17:52,600
Hathai. Where are you going?

250
00:17:52,680 --> 00:17:54,640
Don't you run away from me.

251
00:18:03,120 --> 00:18:05,120
Excuse me. Stop.

252
00:18:05,200 --> 00:18:06,760
Help! Take me to the the alley entrance.

253
00:18:06,840 --> 00:18:08,480
Please.

254
00:18:17,280 --> 00:18:18,880
Sir.

255
00:18:19,520 --> 00:18:22,920
Sir. Please help me.

256
00:18:24,920 --> 00:18:26,800
-Big.
-I warned you.

257
00:18:26,880 --> 00:18:28,760
If you run from me, I'll kill you.

258
00:18:30,360 --> 00:18:32,360
Let go!

259
00:18:36,800 --> 00:18:37,920
Stop!

260
00:18:46,480 --> 00:18:48,560
Was it good, Grandma?

261
00:18:49,680 --> 00:18:51,760
I don't even know what to say.

262
00:18:51,840 --> 00:18:53,880
I'm so full, it's up to my throat.

263
00:18:53,960 --> 00:18:55,800
That full?

264
00:18:55,880 --> 00:18:57,520
Come on. Let's head home.

265
00:18:57,600 --> 00:19:01,400
Wait. I bought some food for Ann.

266
00:19:01,480 --> 00:19:03,720
I left it at the table. I'll go get it.

267
00:19:03,800 --> 00:19:06,560
Absolutely not. I'll get it for you.

268
00:19:07,120 --> 00:19:08,160
Look after her for me.

269
00:19:08,760 --> 00:19:11,080
Sure. But hurry back
and take her off my hands.

270
00:19:11,920 --> 00:19:13,640
You'd like that, wouldn't you?

271
00:19:14,440 --> 00:19:16,240
Just go already.

272
00:19:21,720 --> 00:19:24,080
-Mom?
-Hathaya, help me.

273
00:19:28,800 --> 00:19:30,080
Where have you been?

274
00:19:30,160 --> 00:19:32,240
I've been in Bangkok for a while.

275
00:19:32,320 --> 00:19:35,120
Mom, turn yourself in. Stop running.

276
00:19:35,200 --> 00:19:36,640
You don't have to keep hiding.

277
00:19:36,720 --> 00:19:38,560
I'm not running from the police anymore.

278
00:19:38,640 --> 00:19:41,560
One of Big's contacts pulled strings
and took care of everything.

279
00:19:41,640 --> 00:19:43,280
I'm in the clear now.

280
00:19:44,080 --> 00:19:45,800
Then who are you running from?

281
00:19:45,880 --> 00:19:47,240
Big.

282
00:19:47,320 --> 00:19:49,040
He wants to open another brothel,

283
00:19:49,120 --> 00:19:52,840
but I'm done. Hathaya, please help me.

284
00:19:52,920 --> 00:19:55,360
Let me come live with you. Please.

285
00:20:00,160 --> 00:20:02,440
She's taking a long time.
I should go check.

286
00:20:02,520 --> 00:20:04,520
No, I'll go.

287
00:20:04,600 --> 00:20:07,760
I need to use the restroom anyway.
You wait here.

288
00:20:07,840 --> 00:20:08,920
Are you sure?

289
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:11,640
I can manage. Trust me.

290
00:20:11,720 --> 00:20:13,040
I'll only be a minute.

291
00:20:22,080 --> 00:20:23,840
I know

292
00:20:23,920 --> 00:20:27,200
I've been terrible. I've hurt you.

293
00:20:27,800 --> 00:20:29,520
Please give me one more chance.

294
00:20:29,600 --> 00:20:33,800
I've learned my lesson. I won't get
involved with bad people anymore. Please.

295
00:20:34,520 --> 00:20:36,160
I want to help you.

296
00:20:36,760 --> 00:20:39,200
But I feel terrible imposing on Grandpa.

297
00:20:39,840 --> 00:20:42,920
I know Grandpa doesn't like me.

298
00:20:43,920 --> 00:20:46,320
I'll apologize to him.

299
00:20:46,400 --> 00:20:50,080
I'll work to make up
for everything I've done wrong.

300
00:20:51,400 --> 00:20:53,760
I won't ask for anything.

301
00:20:53,840 --> 00:20:56,880
If he wants me to be a servant,
I'll gladly do it.

302
00:20:57,480 --> 00:20:59,920
I just need a roof over my head.

303
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:02,680
Please let me stay with my daughter.
Hathaya, please.

304
00:21:08,520 --> 00:21:09,800
Hathaya.

305
00:21:10,880 --> 00:21:12,840
You don't love me anymore?

306
00:21:14,280 --> 00:21:17,600
It's me. I'm your mother.

307
00:21:17,680 --> 00:21:20,640
You have to help me. If you don't,

308
00:21:20,720 --> 00:21:24,000
Big is going to kill me.

309
00:21:24,080 --> 00:21:27,560
Please help me. Please.

310
00:21:31,400 --> 00:21:32,800
Please help me.

311
00:21:35,040 --> 00:21:35,960
Mom.

312
00:21:36,480 --> 00:21:38,680
Hathaya, go wait for me at the car.

313
00:21:39,360 --> 00:21:42,400
I need to talk to your mother. Go.

314
00:21:59,000 --> 00:22:00,240
Mom.

315
00:22:07,280 --> 00:22:09,440
Mom, I'm sorry.

316
00:22:12,960 --> 00:22:16,160
I finally understand that Big is terrible.

317
00:22:16,760 --> 00:22:18,360
I'm sorry

318
00:22:19,080 --> 00:22:22,520
I brought someone like him into our home.

319
00:22:22,600 --> 00:22:25,040
He almost killed you.

320
00:22:25,120 --> 00:22:27,320
I'm sorry, Mom.

321
00:22:29,320 --> 00:22:30,840
What do you want?

322
00:22:32,160 --> 00:22:35,080
I want to live with Hathaya.

323
00:22:35,160 --> 00:22:36,600
With you.

324
00:22:37,320 --> 00:22:39,760
The three of us together.

325
00:22:40,800 --> 00:22:42,480
What did Hathaya say?

326
00:22:43,080 --> 00:22:44,640
She hasn't said anything.

327
00:22:46,280 --> 00:22:48,840
I asked to live at Grandpa's house too.

328
00:22:49,760 --> 00:22:52,480
She was almost willing to agree.

329
00:22:53,240 --> 00:22:54,680
I'm happy

330
00:22:54,760 --> 00:22:56,880
you're living with Hathaya.

331
00:22:56,960 --> 00:23:00,120
I want to come back and live
with you and my daughter.

332
00:23:05,720 --> 00:23:07,080
Mom.

333
00:23:07,160 --> 00:23:09,200
Mom? Mom?

334
00:23:09,280 --> 00:23:10,360
Mom?

335
00:23:10,880 --> 00:23:12,480
Mom, what are you doing?

336
00:23:12,560 --> 00:23:14,520
I'm begging you.

337
00:23:14,600 --> 00:23:15,600
Mom?

338
00:23:15,680 --> 00:23:19,600
Please stop ruining your daughter's life.

339
00:23:21,840 --> 00:23:25,400
I know I was wrong.

340
00:23:26,080 --> 00:23:27,640
I'm sorry.

341
00:23:27,720 --> 00:23:30,600
Please give me one more chance
to make things right.

342
00:23:30,680 --> 00:23:32,680
Please, Mom.

343
00:23:33,840 --> 00:23:34,840
Do you know

344
00:23:35,640 --> 00:23:37,160
people in that house

345
00:23:37,240 --> 00:23:41,040
think you taught your daughter
to be deceitful,

346
00:23:41,120 --> 00:23:42,600
to be a bad person?

347
00:23:43,600 --> 00:23:46,160
Hathaya had to keep doing good,

348
00:23:46,240 --> 00:23:49,520
accept everything they put her through,

349
00:23:52,080 --> 00:23:55,560
and prove herself

350
00:23:56,240 --> 00:23:57,560
until they finally saw

351
00:23:57,640 --> 00:23:59,920
who she truly was.

352
00:24:01,960 --> 00:24:03,640
I was shot

353
00:24:03,720 --> 00:24:06,080
and almost died.

354
00:24:06,720 --> 00:24:08,880
But I survived

355
00:24:08,960 --> 00:24:11,440
because of the good Hathaya had done.

356
00:24:13,760 --> 00:24:14,880
Now,

357
00:24:15,560 --> 00:24:17,520
Grandpa loves her.

358
00:24:18,400 --> 00:24:21,760
She has waited her entire life

359
00:24:22,440 --> 00:24:25,560
to be welcomed back into his arms.

360
00:24:26,680 --> 00:24:29,920
Please don't destroy
your daughter's happiness again.

361
00:24:38,840 --> 00:24:40,040
Hathai.

362
00:24:41,920 --> 00:24:44,080
If you still love me

363
00:24:44,760 --> 00:24:47,640
and want to repay me for raising you,

364
00:24:49,000 --> 00:24:51,240
then go live your own life.

365
00:24:52,400 --> 00:24:55,760
Stop holding Hathaya back.

366
00:24:57,280 --> 00:24:58,560
I'm begging you.

367
00:24:58,640 --> 00:25:00,040
Mom.

368
00:25:00,120 --> 00:25:00,960
Mom.

369
00:25:01,040 --> 00:25:04,160
I'm begging you. I truly am.

370
00:25:04,680 --> 00:25:06,560
Mom.

371
00:25:13,480 --> 00:25:16,520
Mom.

372
00:25:17,480 --> 00:25:20,360
I'm begging you.

373
00:25:24,560 --> 00:25:25,440
Grandma.

374
00:25:27,040 --> 00:25:28,000
Grandma.

375
00:25:28,080 --> 00:25:29,560
I feel sorry for Mom.

376
00:25:29,640 --> 00:25:31,400
I'll beg Grandpa

377
00:25:31,480 --> 00:25:34,000
to let her come stay at the house.

378
00:25:34,080 --> 00:25:35,040
Please, Grandma.

379
00:25:35,720 --> 00:25:38,160
Where is Mom? Where did she go?

380
00:25:40,120 --> 00:25:41,160
Your mom left.

381
00:25:43,880 --> 00:25:45,600
Where did she go?

382
00:26:13,680 --> 00:26:14,520
Mom.

383
00:26:16,320 --> 00:26:19,240
I may have been a terrible mother.

384
00:26:21,640 --> 00:26:24,880
But I still have a mother's heart.

385
00:26:28,600 --> 00:26:31,120
I'll go my own way.

386
00:26:33,040 --> 00:26:34,640
But I want you to know.

387
00:26:36,240 --> 00:26:37,640
I admit I was wrong.

388
00:26:38,440 --> 00:26:40,840
And I truly regret what I did.

389
00:26:43,640 --> 00:26:45,400
Please tell Hathaya,

390
00:26:47,320 --> 00:26:50,120
even though I've been a terrible mother,

391
00:26:50,200 --> 00:26:52,680
I love my daughter very much.

392
00:27:21,680 --> 00:27:23,080
I don't understand.

393
00:27:23,840 --> 00:27:26,240
Mom said she wanted to come live with me.

394
00:27:26,960 --> 00:27:29,960
Why did she leave?

395
00:27:31,960 --> 00:27:33,680
Hathai changed her mind.

396
00:27:34,280 --> 00:27:37,280
She feels guilty for causing you
problems all these years.

397
00:27:38,320 --> 00:27:40,920
She doesn't want to be
a burden on you anymore.

398
00:28:10,400 --> 00:28:14,000
-Hey. Where did Ann go?
-I don't know.

399
00:28:14,080 --> 00:28:17,360
How can you not know?
I always see you working with her.

400
00:28:17,440 --> 00:28:19,240
How can you not know where she is? Wait.

401
00:28:19,320 --> 00:28:21,920
Did she sneak out to have fun somewhere?

402
00:28:22,000 --> 00:28:22,840
I don't know.

403
00:28:24,400 --> 00:28:27,080
Or did she take Hathaya's grandmother
out somewhere?

404
00:28:27,160 --> 00:28:28,880
-I don't know.
-Good grief.

405
00:28:28,960 --> 00:28:31,480
Are you a politician?
Every question I ask, you don't know.

406
00:28:31,560 --> 00:28:32,720
I don't know.

407
00:28:32,800 --> 00:28:36,320
Get out of my sight.

408
00:28:36,400 --> 00:28:38,560
If I hear you say that one more time,

409
00:28:38,640 --> 00:28:40,600
I'll slap you until your brain swells.

410
00:28:40,680 --> 00:28:42,120
I don't know.

411
00:28:44,200 --> 00:28:45,200
Hey, beautiful.

412
00:28:46,200 --> 00:28:47,040
Hey, beautiful.

413
00:28:47,920 --> 00:28:49,240
Over here.

414
00:28:58,640 --> 00:29:00,120
Were you calling me?

415
00:29:00,200 --> 00:29:01,640
Yeah.

416
00:29:01,720 --> 00:29:05,120
Do we know each other?

417
00:29:05,200 --> 00:29:06,800
Why are you calling me over?

418
00:29:06,880 --> 00:29:08,080
I wanted to ask--

419
00:29:08,160 --> 00:29:11,520
Ask what? I don't have a boyfriend.

420
00:29:11,600 --> 00:29:14,400
I'm completely single.
I've been single for a long time too.

421
00:29:14,480 --> 00:29:16,360
And if you're going to ask me something,

422
00:29:16,440 --> 00:29:20,480
and I can answer,
what are you giving me in return?

423
00:29:20,560 --> 00:29:23,040
I wanted to ask if Hathai is here.

424
00:29:24,320 --> 00:29:26,880
Hathai? Which Hathai?

425
00:29:26,960 --> 00:29:29,040
Hathai. She used to be
an in-law in this house.

426
00:29:30,280 --> 00:29:31,720
That Hathai?

427
00:29:31,800 --> 00:29:33,560
She was thrown out ages ago.

428
00:29:33,640 --> 00:29:35,920
I know. She told me about it.

429
00:29:36,000 --> 00:29:38,080
I'm her husband.

430
00:29:38,160 --> 00:29:40,040
Her husband?

431
00:29:40,120 --> 00:29:43,760
We had a little argument.
She said she was coming back here.

432
00:29:43,840 --> 00:29:47,000
She told me her daughter
lives in this house.

433
00:29:47,080 --> 00:29:48,440
Can I see her daughter?

434
00:29:48,520 --> 00:29:51,360
Absolutely not.

435
00:29:51,440 --> 00:29:53,840
Now get out. If you don't leave,

436
00:29:53,920 --> 00:29:55,800
I'll call the police to haul you off.

437
00:29:55,880 --> 00:29:58,000
Fine. I'll go.

438
00:29:58,080 --> 00:29:59,560
I'm not scared of you, old hag.

439
00:29:59,640 --> 00:30:02,080
Get out. Go.

440
00:30:03,960 --> 00:30:06,400
Hathai, you can't hide from me.

441
00:30:06,480 --> 00:30:08,760
You're going to work off what you owe me.

442
00:30:10,040 --> 00:30:10,880
Huh?

443
00:30:10,960 --> 00:30:12,280
-Big.
-Old hag!

444
00:30:12,360 --> 00:30:15,320
You're still alive?
I thought you were dead.

445
00:30:17,440 --> 00:30:19,480
Let me go. Let go of me.

446
00:30:19,560 --> 00:30:21,400
-Where's your daughter?
-I don't know.

447
00:30:21,480 --> 00:30:24,480
You came looking for her here.
I came looking for her here too.

448
00:30:24,560 --> 00:30:26,600
She asked to stay with me.

449
00:30:26,680 --> 00:30:29,040
I sent her away.
I don't know where she is.

450
00:30:29,640 --> 00:30:31,440
-Let me go.
-Grandma.

451
00:30:31,520 --> 00:30:34,080
I got everything we needed.

452
00:30:34,160 --> 00:30:36,800
If I find her anywhere,
I'll kill her right there.

453
00:30:40,680 --> 00:30:41,960
Grandma, who was that?

454
00:30:42,040 --> 00:30:44,560
Nobody. He was just asking for directions.

455
00:30:44,640 --> 00:30:45,960
Do you know him?

456
00:30:46,040 --> 00:30:47,920
No. Come on.

457
00:30:48,000 --> 00:30:49,520
Let's get inside.

458
00:31:03,800 --> 00:31:04,960
Grandma.

459
00:31:05,840 --> 00:31:09,000
Your beautiful granddaughter is home.

460
00:31:17,840 --> 00:31:18,800
Grandma,

461
00:31:20,400 --> 00:31:22,320
is something bothering you?

462
00:31:24,320 --> 00:31:25,640
No.

463
00:31:27,400 --> 00:31:28,480
Grandma,

464
00:31:29,480 --> 00:31:31,120
don't lie to me.

465
00:31:31,800 --> 00:31:34,800
Aunt Ann said
you've barely eaten anything.

466
00:31:36,240 --> 00:31:37,800
What's bothering you?

467
00:31:43,720 --> 00:31:44,840
Hathaya.

468
00:31:46,080 --> 00:31:48,320
I was the one who sent your mom away.

469
00:31:50,560 --> 00:31:52,200
Someone like her

470
00:31:52,280 --> 00:31:55,440
will probably never truly change.

471
00:31:56,040 --> 00:31:57,640
That's why I sent her away.

472
00:31:58,520 --> 00:32:01,680
I didn't want her
causing you any more problems.

473
00:32:03,040 --> 00:32:06,840
But this morning, Big came here.

474
00:32:07,640 --> 00:32:09,880
He threatened to kill Hathai.

475
00:32:13,760 --> 00:32:16,800
Grandma, I'm worried about Mom.

476
00:32:17,720 --> 00:32:19,720
Can we go find her?

477
00:32:19,800 --> 00:32:21,880
Then we can
bring her back to live with us.

478
00:32:23,640 --> 00:32:24,600
Please, Grandma.

479
00:32:44,920 --> 00:32:45,840
Help!

480
00:32:45,920 --> 00:32:47,600
Mom, help!

481
00:32:54,920 --> 00:32:58,000
Stay here!

482
00:33:06,840 --> 00:33:09,000
Is this Hathaya?

483
00:33:09,920 --> 00:33:12,240
Grandma, Mom sent me a message.

484
00:33:13,000 --> 00:33:14,320
What does she want now?

485
00:33:14,400 --> 00:33:15,640
I'm calling her back.

486
00:33:23,240 --> 00:33:24,520
Hathaya.

487
00:33:25,680 --> 00:33:29,800
Mom. It's Hathaya.
I'm with Grandma right now.

488
00:33:30,480 --> 00:33:32,280
I'm sorry, sweetheart.

489
00:33:34,280 --> 00:33:36,160
I've been a terrible mother.

490
00:33:38,680 --> 00:33:40,160
Ever since you were born,

491
00:33:41,000 --> 00:33:43,560
I've never done anything
to make you proud.

492
00:33:45,960 --> 00:33:50,280
I kept trying to make
our lives comfortable.

493
00:33:50,360 --> 00:33:53,240
I kept trying to make up for my mistakes.

494
00:33:55,000 --> 00:33:58,120
But the more I tried,
the more I ruined everything.

495
00:34:01,040 --> 00:34:03,720
I have no excuses.

496
00:34:06,320 --> 00:34:08,400
My life is worthless.

497
00:34:10,199 --> 00:34:11,920
Even you grandmother,

498
00:34:12,000 --> 00:34:14,159
my own mother,

499
00:34:14,960 --> 00:34:17,960
rejected me.

500
00:34:18,639 --> 00:34:19,719
Hathai.

501
00:34:20,400 --> 00:34:23,960
We need to talk. Where are you?

502
00:34:25,239 --> 00:34:26,600
Mom.

503
00:34:29,600 --> 00:34:30,960
Mom.

504
00:34:34,000 --> 00:34:35,800
I admit it.

505
00:34:36,880 --> 00:34:39,080
I used to resent you

506
00:34:39,159 --> 00:34:41,800
for making me grow up poor.

507
00:34:43,360 --> 00:34:46,360
I wanted a better life.

508
00:34:46,440 --> 00:34:48,639
A comfortable life.

509
00:34:51,520 --> 00:34:53,360
But I was blind.

510
00:34:54,120 --> 00:34:56,760
I became obsessed with wealth.

511
00:34:56,840 --> 00:34:59,800
I couldn't see your love or everything

512
00:34:59,880 --> 00:35:02,000
you sacrificed for me.

513
00:35:02,080 --> 00:35:03,760
I'm sorry.

514
00:35:07,520 --> 00:35:09,680
I'm sorry.

515
00:35:12,400 --> 00:35:14,880
Mom, where are you?

516
00:35:14,960 --> 00:35:16,840
Grandma and I will come get you.

517
00:35:17,680 --> 00:35:19,160
Hathaya,

518
00:35:20,120 --> 00:35:23,680
don't let me become another burden on you.

519
00:35:24,920 --> 00:35:26,800
I called to say goodbye.

520
00:35:28,000 --> 00:35:31,080
Hathai. Listen to me first.

521
00:35:32,320 --> 00:35:33,400
Mom,

522
00:35:34,440 --> 00:35:37,080
please forgive me for everything.

523
00:35:41,560 --> 00:35:44,120
If there really is a next life,

524
00:35:46,560 --> 00:35:47,480
I…

525
00:35:50,560 --> 00:35:51,480
I…

526
00:35:52,400 --> 00:35:55,920
want to be born again so I can
make up for everything I did wrong.

527
00:35:58,000 --> 00:36:00,880
I'll be a good daughter to you

528
00:36:01,760 --> 00:36:04,760
and a good mother to my child.

529
00:36:06,080 --> 00:36:08,280
Goodbye, Mom.

530
00:36:08,360 --> 00:36:10,840
Mom. Don't.

531
00:36:10,920 --> 00:36:12,760
Don't do anything drastic.

532
00:36:12,840 --> 00:36:15,360
Please don't hurt yourself.

533
00:36:17,200 --> 00:36:20,360
Hathai. Listen to me.

534
00:36:33,800 --> 00:36:36,360
-Hathai.
-Mom.

535
00:36:36,440 --> 00:36:37,920
Mom.

536
00:36:47,520 --> 00:36:48,880
-Mom.
-Hathai.

537
00:36:51,400 --> 00:36:52,440
Mom.

538
00:36:57,800 --> 00:36:59,240
Mom.

539
00:37:01,320 --> 00:37:03,680
Mom. I love you.

540
00:37:03,760 --> 00:37:05,520
Please be okay.

541
00:37:05,600 --> 00:37:08,200
Come back and live with me.

542
00:37:08,840 --> 00:37:10,640
I love you.

543
00:37:10,720 --> 00:37:12,840
I forgive you.

544
00:37:13,920 --> 00:37:15,840
You don't have to wait
until your next life.

545
00:37:17,520 --> 00:37:20,440
You have to stay alive
and make things right in this one.

546
00:37:21,080 --> 00:37:25,000
You have to stay
and take care of me until the day I die.

547
00:37:39,360 --> 00:37:43,120
Mom, are you listening to me?

548
00:37:43,200 --> 00:37:44,280
Hello?

549
00:37:44,360 --> 00:37:45,760
Hathai.

550
00:37:45,840 --> 00:37:48,360
You have to keep fighting.

551
00:37:50,280 --> 00:37:53,400
I'll live. I'll fight.

552
00:37:55,720 --> 00:37:57,840
I'll stay alive. I'll fight, sweetheart.

553
00:38:05,800 --> 00:38:07,760
I'll go back and start over.

554
00:38:07,840 --> 00:38:10,480
I'm going to make things right.

555
00:38:34,000 --> 00:38:36,600
Grandma, Mom sent her location.

556
00:38:36,680 --> 00:38:40,240
We'll go get her.
I'll have Ramil drive us.

557
00:38:59,360 --> 00:39:02,240
Mom sent this location.
She must be somewhere around here.

558
00:39:02,960 --> 00:39:05,000
Let's split up and look. I'll go that way.

559
00:39:05,080 --> 00:39:06,200
Yes.

560
00:39:06,280 --> 00:39:08,520
Grandma, let's go find Mom.

561
00:39:15,160 --> 00:39:19,280
Mom. Grandma and I are here.
Where are you?

562
00:39:21,120 --> 00:39:23,680
Mom? Where are you?

563
00:39:30,640 --> 00:39:32,040
Hathaya?

564
00:39:34,480 --> 00:39:35,200
Big.

565
00:39:35,280 --> 00:39:37,600
Let me go. Let me go right now.

566
00:39:37,680 --> 00:39:39,680
I told you I'm done.

567
00:39:39,760 --> 00:39:41,200
Let me go.

568
00:39:41,280 --> 00:39:44,440
I told you already. You can't escape me.

569
00:39:44,520 --> 00:39:48,800
You know all my secrets.
If you betray me, I'll get arrested.

570
00:39:48,880 --> 00:39:51,200
I'll swear on anything you want.

571
00:39:51,280 --> 00:39:54,480
I'll never get involved. Just let me go.
We'll go our separate ways.

572
00:39:54,560 --> 00:39:56,320
Stop. Stop!

573
00:39:56,400 --> 00:39:57,720
Don't hurt my mom.

574
00:39:57,800 --> 00:39:59,920
Hathaya, help me.

575
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:02,480
Let go of my daughter.
Let her go right now.

576
00:40:02,560 --> 00:40:04,200
-At first…
-Grandma, don't.

577
00:40:04,280 --> 00:40:07,200
I only wanted revenge on your daughter
for trying to leave me.

578
00:40:07,280 --> 00:40:09,720
But then I saw
the house you people live in.

579
00:40:09,800 --> 00:40:11,320
I changed my mind.

580
00:40:11,400 --> 00:40:14,120
Go get me ten million baht,

581
00:40:14,200 --> 00:40:15,800
then I'll let her go.

582
00:40:16,480 --> 00:40:19,680
I only work there.
I don't have that kind of money.

583
00:40:19,760 --> 00:40:21,880
Then find it. Or she dies.

584
00:40:21,960 --> 00:40:24,320
Please don't hurt my mother.

585
00:40:24,400 --> 00:40:25,880
I'm begging you.

586
00:40:25,960 --> 00:40:27,560
Steal if you have to. I don't care.

587
00:40:27,640 --> 00:40:29,360
Bring me ten million tonight.

588
00:40:29,440 --> 00:40:32,080
Otherwise, you can come
collect your mother's body.

589
00:40:32,160 --> 00:40:35,880
Okay. Okay. Just don't hurt her.

590
00:40:35,960 --> 00:40:40,680
Please. I only have
a few million available right now.

591
00:40:40,760 --> 00:40:43,680
Let my mom go,

592
00:40:43,760 --> 00:40:47,120
and I'll get you the rest.

593
00:40:47,200 --> 00:40:49,680
Fine. Then transfer
everything you have to me.

594
00:40:49,760 --> 00:40:51,520
What's your account number?

595
00:40:52,120 --> 00:40:53,280
Hathaya.

596
00:40:56,280 --> 00:40:57,240
Let me go!

597
00:40:57,320 --> 00:40:59,080
-Run. Hathaya, run.
-Grandma!

598
00:40:59,160 --> 00:41:01,000
Mom, go! Quickly!

599
00:41:01,080 --> 00:41:02,440
Careful, Mom.

600
00:41:06,800 --> 00:41:08,680
-Come on.
-Walk carefully.

601
00:41:08,760 --> 00:41:10,400
Walk carefully.

602
00:41:12,560 --> 00:41:13,920
-Big.
-Hathai.

603
00:41:14,000 --> 00:41:15,680
No!

604
00:41:15,760 --> 00:41:18,080
-Mom.
-Grandma.

605
00:41:18,160 --> 00:41:21,400
You try to outsmart me,
your whole damn family dies.

606
00:41:22,520 --> 00:41:23,440
Grandma.

607
00:41:23,520 --> 00:41:25,400
-Mom.
-Grandma.

608
00:41:26,280 --> 00:41:28,760
-Mom.
-Grandma.

609
00:41:31,800 --> 00:41:33,840
You haven't seen the last of me.

610
00:41:35,200 --> 00:41:36,280
Mom.

611
00:41:36,880 --> 00:41:40,040
-Mom.
-Grandma.

612
00:41:40,120 --> 00:41:42,120
-Grandma.
-Mom.

613
00:41:42,200 --> 00:41:44,000
Please be okay.

614
00:41:44,080 --> 00:41:46,200
I'm taking you to the hospital.

615
00:41:47,000 --> 00:41:49,760
-I need an ambulance immediately.
-You'll be fine, Mom.

616
00:41:51,600 --> 00:41:53,760
There's no need, sweetheart.

617
00:41:54,680 --> 00:41:57,440
This is as far as my merit can take me.

618
00:41:59,360 --> 00:42:00,400
No, Mom.

619
00:42:01,280 --> 00:42:02,240
Mom.

620
00:42:03,120 --> 00:42:05,600
You're too tough to die.

621
00:42:05,680 --> 00:42:07,480
You survived once already.

622
00:42:07,560 --> 00:42:09,560
You have to stay with me.

623
00:42:13,600 --> 00:42:17,200
I traded my merit for your life.

624
00:42:19,280 --> 00:42:21,680
No, Mom.

625
00:42:21,760 --> 00:42:24,120
Don't blame yourself.

626
00:42:25,520 --> 00:42:27,720
You told me

627
00:42:27,800 --> 00:42:29,800
you were going to become a new person.

628
00:42:30,880 --> 00:42:32,560
You can do it.

629
00:42:33,680 --> 00:42:35,680
You have to be strong.

630
00:42:38,520 --> 00:42:41,880
I'm sorry I rejected you

631
00:42:41,960 --> 00:42:43,960
and drove you away before.

632
00:42:45,720 --> 00:42:48,400
But I'm glad

633
00:42:49,200 --> 00:42:52,160
I had the chance to make it right.

634
00:42:52,840 --> 00:42:55,600
-Mom.
-Grandma.

635
00:42:56,400 --> 00:42:59,560
You don't have to wait
until your next life.

636
00:43:00,600 --> 00:43:01,720
You can still

637
00:43:02,440 --> 00:43:06,200
be a good mother in this one.

638
00:43:08,840 --> 00:43:10,800
Take care

639
00:43:10,880 --> 00:43:12,160
of Hathaya for me.

640
00:43:12,240 --> 00:43:13,480
Grandma.

641
00:43:15,600 --> 00:43:18,600
I promise, Mom. I promise.

642
00:43:19,920 --> 00:43:22,280
I'll take good care of my daughter.

643
00:43:23,400 --> 00:43:25,920
I'll give my life for her,

644
00:43:26,000 --> 00:43:28,480
just like you did for me.

645
00:43:32,360 --> 00:43:33,600
Grandma.

646
00:43:37,920 --> 00:43:39,880
When I'm gone,

647
00:43:40,560 --> 00:43:43,440
you have to take good care of yourself.

648
00:43:43,520 --> 00:43:45,720
No.

649
00:43:45,800 --> 00:43:48,040
Nothing is going to happen to you.

650
00:43:48,120 --> 00:43:51,360
The three of us are supposed
to finally be together.

651
00:43:51,440 --> 00:43:53,520
Don't talk like this.

652
00:43:55,600 --> 00:43:58,520
Your mom is back with you now.

653
00:43:59,240 --> 00:44:02,280
You won't be alone anymore.

654
00:44:05,680 --> 00:44:07,840
You…

655
00:44:07,920 --> 00:44:11,080
take good care of Grandpa.

656
00:44:12,920 --> 00:44:15,600
Pay attention to him.

657
00:44:16,960 --> 00:44:19,160
Old people

658
00:44:19,960 --> 00:44:22,080
may sometimes have sharp tongues,

659
00:44:23,720 --> 00:44:25,200
but our hearts

660
00:44:25,800 --> 00:44:27,680
are fragile.

661
00:44:28,960 --> 00:44:31,200
Look after him carefully, sweetheart.

662
00:44:32,640 --> 00:44:34,840
I'm asking you.

663
00:44:36,720 --> 00:44:37,680
Grandma…

664
00:44:39,640 --> 00:44:41,680
Grandma…

665
00:44:46,160 --> 00:44:50,400
I finally figured out
what I wanted to cook for Grandpa.

666
00:44:52,520 --> 00:44:55,960
Make it for him for me.

667
00:44:56,040 --> 00:44:57,680
No. No.

668
00:44:57,760 --> 00:45:01,080
I'm not accepting this.
I won't do it for you.

669
00:45:01,160 --> 00:45:03,800
Grandpa is going to eat your cooking.

670
00:45:04,640 --> 00:45:07,880
You have to make it for him yourself.

671
00:45:09,360 --> 00:45:11,160
Grandma.

672
00:45:16,360 --> 00:45:19,080
I've been so happy

673
00:45:20,000 --> 00:45:22,640
to have had the chance
to take care of you.

674
00:45:26,400 --> 00:45:27,960
Grandma.

675
00:45:28,040 --> 00:45:31,560
Remember what I taught you.

676
00:45:33,240 --> 00:45:36,440
We can't choose how we're born.

677
00:45:38,040 --> 00:45:41,360
But we can choose

678
00:45:42,240 --> 00:45:44,440
to be good people.

679
00:45:48,680 --> 00:45:50,880
-Mom. Mom!
-Grandma.

680
00:45:51,840 --> 00:45:54,080
-Mom.
-Grandma.

681
00:45:54,160 --> 00:45:56,160
Grandma, please!

682
00:46:04,440 --> 00:46:06,680
-Grandma!
-Mom!

683
00:46:07,520 --> 00:46:09,680
-Grandma!
-Mom!

684
00:46:17,640 --> 00:46:18,880
Grandma!

685
00:46:43,200 --> 00:46:44,560
Hello, sir.

686
00:46:45,800 --> 00:46:48,560
Ramil, where does the case stand?

687
00:46:49,160 --> 00:46:51,440
Big is facing very serious charges.

688
00:46:51,520 --> 00:46:55,280
The lawyer said he'll likely
receive the maximum sentence.

689
00:46:55,960 --> 00:46:58,240
The world is driven by karma.

690
00:46:58,840 --> 00:47:00,960
All beings must live
according to their karma.

691
00:47:01,920 --> 00:47:05,280
Whatever karma someone creates,
they must eventually face consequences.

692
00:47:07,040 --> 00:47:08,840
How is Hathaya?

693
00:47:45,840 --> 00:47:47,680
I'm not going to tell you not to cry.

694
00:47:53,080 --> 00:47:54,840
I want you to stay

695
00:47:56,360 --> 00:47:58,520
with your memories of Grandma Duangjai.

696
00:48:01,080 --> 00:48:02,800
And I want you

697
00:48:04,880 --> 00:48:06,600
to let all of your grief out.

698
00:48:14,480 --> 00:48:17,240
Right now, you probably
feel like your whole world

699
00:48:18,440 --> 00:48:19,440
has collapsed.

700
00:48:22,440 --> 00:48:24,640
It was like that for me

701
00:48:26,720 --> 00:48:28,440
when my father left me

702
00:48:30,360 --> 00:48:32,200
and my mother started a new family.

703
00:48:34,400 --> 00:48:36,360
I felt

704
00:48:37,760 --> 00:48:41,040
completely alone. Like I had nothing left.

705
00:48:58,000 --> 00:49:00,240
It's Hathai. Hathaya's mother.

706
00:49:00,320 --> 00:49:01,960
She's already come into the house.

707
00:49:02,040 --> 00:49:03,640
Then what do you want me to do?

708
00:49:03,720 --> 00:49:05,280
Kneel and bow to me.

709
00:49:05,360 --> 00:49:08,760
NEXT EPISODE

710
00:49:08,840 --> 00:49:10,040
What are you doing?

711
00:49:11,240 --> 00:49:13,600
If you like things spicy,

712
00:49:13,680 --> 00:49:16,880
then I'll pour some curry
and make it really burn.

713
00:49:20,040 --> 00:49:22,440
-Chayanee.
-Don't raise your voice at me.

714
00:49:22,520 --> 00:49:24,680
Did Chayanee say something that upset you?

715
00:51:22,480 --> 00:51:24,400
Subtitle translation by: Thanit Puncharoen
